    {
      "title": "TSMC's record AI chip profits come with a hidden tax that every founder should understand - Startup Fortune",
      "date": "2026-07-22",
      "source": "Startup Fortune",
      "url": "https://startupfortune.com/tsmcs-record-ai-chip-profits-come-with-a-hidden-tax-that-every-founder-should-understand/",
      "summary": "TSMC's record AI chip profits come with a hidden tax that every founder should understand Startup Fortune",
      "body": "TSMC's record quarter came with a cost warning founders shouldn't ignore: the AI supply chain is getting more expensive at the base, and some of that pressure will work its way up.\nThe numbers from TSMC's second quarter looked almost absurdly good. Revenue hit $40.2 billion, up 33.7% year over year, according to the company's July 16 earnings materials. Gross margin reached 67.7%. Operating margin hit 60.3%. For the company making the chips behind Nvidia's AI accelerators, Apple's silicon, AMD processors and a long list of cloud hardware, this wasn't a soft quarter dressed up by accounting language.\nThen TSMC started talking about what it costs to keep building.\nWendell Huang, TSMC's senior vice president and chief financial officer, told investors on the July 16 earnings call that overseas fabs are already diluting margins, even with demand running hot. He said TSMC still expects the ramp-up of overseas fabs to dilute gross margin by 2% to 3% in the early stages and widen to 3% to 4% ",
