      "title": "Samsung's DRAM dominance looks safe despite CXMT's expansion plans - SamMobile",
      "date": "2026-07-22",
      "source": "SamMobile",
      "url": "https://www.sammobile.com/news/samsung-dram-dominance-looks-safe-despite-cxmt-expansion/",
      "summary": "Samsung's DRAM dominance looks safe despite CXMT's expansion plans SamMobile",
      "body": "Last updated: July 22nd, 2026 at 14:15 UTC+02:00\nIt is forecasted to have a 34% share in the DRAM market in 2028.\nAbhijeet Mishra / SamMobile\nSince the demand for artificial intelligence (AI) started rising exponentially over the past few years, the need for the hardware required to power it, especially memory chips, has also increased significantly.\nWith demand for memory outpacing supply, memory chip makers around the world have been raising the prices of their products. Samsung, being the world's largest memory chip manufacturer, has been one of the biggest beneficiaries of this trend.\nHowever, seeing the soaring demand and thick profits, China's CXMT has decided to significantly expand its presence in the memory market. While the Chinese company is expected to grow rapidly, a new forecast about the DRAM market suggests that CXMT is unlikely to dethrone Samsung anytime soon or even have a significant impact on the South Korean tech giant.\nAccording to a new report from Counterpoint ",
